## Summary — S519 (open item 4: census A_k without enumeration)

I answered the NEXT ACTION: count A_k by a transfer matrix instead of enumerating all ~A_k patterns, validate bit-for-bit, push toward k=128 **or** prove the state space is exponential. The result is the latter (the explicitly-offered deliverable), plus two structural facts that *do* scale.

**Built** `experiments/analytic/local_pattern_census/census_transfer_matrix.py` (one script, `--selftest`/`--k`/`--scan`/`--reduce`, 9 selftest groups; TM reproduces every known A_k bit-for-bit, `brute == DFS == TM`).

**(1) Transfer-matrix route CLOSED.** The natural position-DP — state = per-prime occupied-residue *set*, with fully-covered primes pruned as absorbing dead states — has **Θ(A_k) distinct states**. Measured collapse factor `A_k/states = 1.86, 1.66, 2.37, 1.55` at k=8,16,32,64 (bounded, not growing); `ln(states)` slope **1.020** ≈ `ln A_k` slope **1.011**. Same entropy exponent ⇒ exponential, and *strictly worse* than the existing DFS (Θ(A_k) memory vs Θ(k); the final live-state count is offset-ordering-independent ≈ A_k/2). k=128 (A₁₂₈≈10¹¹) is unreachable by either; inclusion-exclusion has the known catastrophic cancellation. No new exact A_k value is obtainable — stated honestly.

**(2) Active-prime reduction (rigorous, two independent agreeing proofs — count-stabilization and a no-count W(B) branch-and-bound min-union).** A_k depends only on primes ≤ B(k): **B(k) = 3,5,7,13,23,47** at k=8,16,32,64,128,256. **A₁₂₈ uses only 8 primes {3,5,7,11,13,17,19,23}**; the 9 larger enforceable primes provably never bind.

**(3) Identity W(B(k)) = ρ*(k) = maximal admissible-tuple size** = 3,5,9,16,28,52 — the weight bound is tight, so it equals the densest admissible aligned-k tuple, **matching the classical H() (OEIS A008407) exactly** at k=64 (H(16)=60<H(17)=66) and k=128 (H(28)=126<H(29)=132). With ρ*/(k/ln k) = 0.78→1.13, this explains *why* `ln A_k = Θ(π(k))` — admissibles live in the ρ*(k)≈k/ln k geometry. The entropy slope→1 (1.01) is re-confirmed independently of the DFS.

